/-! ## The half-closed cubes tile `ℝ^d`

"For technical reasons, we need the property that every `x` in `ℝ^d` is
contained in some cube. Therefore we consider half-closed cubes." The cubes
`Ã_h(x)`, `x ∈ hℤ^d`, do tile: every point lies in exactly one. -/

/-! ## Lemma 3.4 -/

theorem QFS.lemma_cubes {h : ℝ} (hh : 0 < h) {x y s t : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)}
    (hx : x ∈ scaledLattice d h) (hy : y ∈ scaledLattice d h)
    (hxy : Real.sqrt d * h < ‖x - y‖) (hs : s ∈ cube h x) (ht : t ∈ cube h y) :
    1 / (2 * Real.sqrt d) * ‖x - y‖ < ‖s - t‖ ∧ ‖s - t‖ < 2 * Real.sqrt d * ‖x - y‖ := by sorry
